    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a gauntlet today against Cease, whose 2.96 xERA dictates a high-caution approach. Consequently, our offensive output is limited to two marginal plays: **Drake Baldwin** (40.04) and **Andy Pages** (42.71). Both hitters are suppressed by the opposing ace\u2019s elite skill profile and unfavorable batting order slots (#9 and #8, respectively). While **Andy Pages** retains a slight edge due to his better xwOBA metrics, neither player projects for more than a neutral impact. We are heavily reliant on them avoiding negative regression against a high-strikeout arm, as the lack of volume in the bottom third of the order restricts their counting stat potential in this 5x5 format.\n\nThe remainder of our roster, including stalwarts like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, are inactive due to scheduled team off-days. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains our primary health concern, sidelined on the IL. With no active games for the core of the lineup, the optimizer\u2019s bench decisions were straightforward; **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** would typically anchor our production, but they provide zero value today alongside the likes of **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Denzer Guzman**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Cole Carrigg**. We are effectively treating today as a preservation day for game caps, prioritizing the safety of our remaining starts while waiting for the full squad to return to action.",
